WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.250
Laugh Tale and the one piece have been swallowed
by a gigantic island whale, one of Laboon's

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:10.330
brothers, who took a big chunk out of Jaya,
where there is now this big whole.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:15.010
That Whale has been trapped by the world government
at the bottom of the giant whirlpool between

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:26.029
the three gates of justice and the three most
guarded government facilities in the world.

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:31.289
What gets you to that conclusion is that Whales
in One Piece always, ALWAYS appear whenever

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:33.590
Laugh Tale and the one piece are mentioned.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:39.870
Or to be more precise, I realized that whales
guide Luffy and the straw hats towards the

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.510
right direction.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:46.300
This starts as early as chapter 8, where we
see a whale fountain in Orange Town, just

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.760
as Nami acquires the map of the grand line
from Buggy.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:56.400
Then, we have arguably the most important
scene in the entire story, as we meet Laboon

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:03.850
at the entrance of said grand line.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.469
[] I just love that whale.

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:06.469
So cute.

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:11.539
Now, I personally am CONVINCED, that Laboon
is the key to figuring out the true nature

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:12.710
of laugh tale.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:17.679
First of all, the whale is once again connected
to finding the right direction to laugh tale,

00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:22.119
because it is here where the straw hats get
the log pose from Crocus, who later turns

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:28.520
out has been a member of the Roger pirates
himself who has actually been to laugh tale.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:35.240
Something I still consider to be one of the
most underrated reveals in the entire story.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.229
Crocus not only explains to the crew how to
navigate the grand line properly, but more

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:51.569
importantly is the first one to reveal the
name of the final island, laugh tale.

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:56.250
What's up my name is Manu and I cant even
begin to tell you how excited I am about this

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.439
theory today.

00:01:57.439 --> 00:02:01.509
The more I looked into it, the more it blew
my mind.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:06.999
Now I highly doubt Crocus revels this info
to anyone who tries to enter the grand line.

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:12.930
In fact he did so, only after Luffy managed
to befriend Laboon and keep him from hitting

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.920
his head against the red line.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.110
However, If you have watched any of my other
videos, you will know that I don't believe

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.580
this to be a simply act of kindness.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:27.280
I strongly believe that Crocus was placed
at the entrance to the grand line by his former

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:33.110
captain Roger to wait for the right person
to find Laugh Tale and the One PIece.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:39.060
Not only does Luffy say the same things as
Roger and is incredibly kind and caring towards

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:44.690
Laboon, but he also wears the straw hat, that
used to belong to Roger, which immediately

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:51.100
tells crocus that this is the man they have
been waiting for.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.400
That is why he tells Luffy about laugh tale.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.480
But we're not done with Laboon.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.760
Because the first thing that happens to the
straw hats when entering the grand line is

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:06.610
getting swallowed by this enormous whale.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:13.940
It'a a reference to the classic story trope
of Jonah and the whale, that can for example

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:18.370
also be found in Pinocchio, who also gets
swallowed by a whale and who leaves the whale

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.450
a changed person.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:25.220
Similarly, I think it's more than fair to
say that the straw hats leave Laboon changed,

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.660
now worthy of sailing towards the final island.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:35.980
Laboon himself is so gigantic, that, as you
hopefully remember, he actually has an island

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:41.620
INSIDE of him, from where crocus tries to
take care of him, the first island of the

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.550
grand line.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:49.700
This is where the idea comes from that the
last island might be inside a whale as well.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.460
As far as I know, people have made the connection
between whales and Laugh Tale quite early,

00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:00.010
but this theory in particular stems from my
favorite Japanese one piece YouTuber Yuderon,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.490
who's ideas I have already talked about in
two other massive videos.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:10.990
According to Yuderon, and I personally 100%
believe that he's spot on with this, Eiichiro

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:16.590
Oda, the author of One Piece, writes his story
according to three core principles.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.760
Symbolism, Two sides of the same coin and
word plays.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.100
The symbol here is of course the whale that
represents the journey to Laugh tale, but

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:29.350
what I want you to focus on is the second
concept.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:35.060
Oda takes elements and concepts of before
the time skip, and reintroduces them after

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.090
the time skip in an inverted or mirrored way.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:56.430
Which I find an ingeniously smart way to structure
a long-format story like one piece.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.810
If you want to learn more about this, I suggest
you check out my other videos with Yuderon

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:04.070
on this topic, but here's A quick example
to illustrate this:

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:10.090
Alabasta and dressrosa are both arcs about
a warlord that rules from the shadow over

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:11.280
a country.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:17.000
Both are manipulative, run an underground
organisation and have to be exposed and defeated

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.060
by Luffy.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.840
Both times we have a princess that tries to
help her country.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.150
The kings of the countries are unable to help
their people.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:32.639
The marines are there to interfere, but finally
relaize that Luffy is trying to help.

00:05:32.639 --> 00:05:34.520
And much much more.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:39.980
Well the argument here, is that the first
and last island of the grand line will also

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.270
mirror each other.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.740
An island inside a giant whale.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.870
Not only do we know right from the start,
that this is actually possible, but the person

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:59.500
who created the island actually has been to
laugh tale itself.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.980
So to me at least, it would make a ton of
sense, if Crocus got inspiration for this

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.960
from the final island itself.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.960
Don't you think?

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.639
Then, there's the name of Laboon's species.

00:06:10.639 --> 00:06:14.690
He is a literal island whale.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:19.630
That felt very much like in your face writing
by Oda-sensei once I started to look at that

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.350
scene again from this perspective.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:26.870
And we know that laboon is still relatively
young in island whale years, so there most

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:30.389
likely are even larger relatives of his out
there.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:34.840
Now in general, if you love mythology and
fantasy as much as I do, you will probably

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:35.840
know that the concept of giant whales with
islands is a very famous trope.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.680
Tales of gigantuous whales with islands on
their back are very common and part of folk

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.870
lore all over the world.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:48.430
So it's not exactly mysterious where Oda-sensei
might have gotten this idea from.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:54.260
I have even more to say about Laboon, but
let's look at the other whale symbolism throughout

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.680
one piece first.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.470
If you look closely, we have small whales
engraved in the gates of the palace in alabasta,

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:05.720
that is tied close to the void century, one
of the ancient weapons and is right above

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:07.100
the hidden poneglyph.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:13.229
Similarly, there are whales engraved on the
giant golden bell in the lost city of shandora.

00:07:13.229 --> 00:07:18.250
Not only is this city connected to the ancient
kingdom, but according to the big theory of

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:23.250
Yuderon, actually was part of the ancient
kingdom on Jaya.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.460
Oh and doesn't this on top here look a lot
like a monkey with a straw hat to you?

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.460
Just saying.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:34.880
Then, we have whitebeards ship, the Moby dick
appearing at Marineford, as the emperor declares

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:46.550
that the one piece is real []. 
We see whales in chapter 604, just before

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:51.450
crossing the red line and reaching fishman
island, that is connected to joy boy and is

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.600
home to one of the ancient weapons.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:08:00.870
And by the way, there are also whales, when
robin deciphers the poneglyph there.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:01.870
[]

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:07.740
Then, after leaving fishman island and entering
the new world, the straw hats are welcomed

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:13.050
by a pod of island whales, mirroring their
encounter with laboon and marking their progress

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.330
towards finding the last island.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:21.210
After that it takes a while for a whale to
appear again, but it finally happens on Zou,

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:27.070
where there is a giant whale shaped tree,
that contains the first road poneglyph pointing

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:33.880
the direction to laugh tale.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.150
[] I think its also worth mentioning, that
Zunesha herself is connected to the whale

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.820
theory very closely.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:45.700
I think Oda took the classic idea of a whale
with an island on its back and turned it into

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.670
an elephant, that is also closely connected
to the void century.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:55.190
It proves to me, that having a giant creature
that harbours an entire island is very much

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:56.190
possible.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:01.730
Zuneshia has been tasked with walking to a
certain location as punishment for her sin,

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:05.650
so could she be looking for a giant whale?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:11.589
Also I just realized, that the road poneglyph
is literally inside the giant whale again.

00:09:11.589 --> 00:09:13.830
Almost too obvious Oda-sensei.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:19.050
So as you can see, the whale symbol is closely
connected to anything to do with the ancient

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.130
kingdom and the void century.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:27.160
Alabasta, shandora, Fishman island, Zou - the
only place left is Wano.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:31.300
But, there haven't been any whales on Wano
have there?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.660
You might like this one.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:34.970
Take a look at the Kozuki crest.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.010
Of course the main theme here is the crane
in the middle.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.860
But what do you think about the crossbones
around it?

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:46.970
To me, they look a lot like whale fins diving
into the sea.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.930
Very hard to unsee, am I right?

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:54.840
Now this might just be a way for Oda, to connect
all these places, but I think it's quite possible

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:58.490
that the whale itself was the symbol of the
ancient kingdom.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:03.730
I mean the chapter itself is titled 'Inside
the whale'.

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:07.540
But let's get back to the giant whale that
holds laugh tale.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:12.220
Because there is a lot more evidence that
there is a twin whale to laboon, another whale

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:16.860
just like him, that has also eaten an entire
island.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:20.680
First of all, the place where Laboon was introduced
is called Twin Capes.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:26.830
Then have the giant kraken surume who lives
at the bottom of the ocean and who has a brother,

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:38.940
that was held hostage by Holy and thus forced
him to comply.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:43.690
Could this hint at Laboon's relative being
held hostage by the world government?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:52.490
We also get this interesting line by the sea
kings.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:53.490
[]

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:59.180
But the most important chapter, after the
encounter with Laboon, is 654, where the straw

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.610
hats arrive in the new world.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:07.820
The chapter starts with Luffy catching a fish
that is swallowed another fish, swallowed

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.080
by an even larger fish.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:16.200
The chapter is titled a pod of whales and
on the cover features the twins moz and kiwi

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:22.890
from water seven, the risky brothers as well
as Lola, who we now know also has a twin sister

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:23.940
with chiffon.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:29.640
Oh and the chapter also features an enormous
whirlpool, that transports the straw hats

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:35.060
right to a huge pod of island whales.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:43.500
And this is where things get really interesting,
as you can see, I cant stop grinning when

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.550
thinking about it.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:49.550
In this same chapter, we get reminded that
Laboon is closely tied to one of the straw

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.870
hats in particular.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:12:03.660
Brook, the musician of the crew, who had this
tear-jerking flashback with 

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.660
the whale.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.970
[] In this chapter, Brook of course mistakes
the whales for lagoon and starts singing the

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.540
song that always made laboon happy when he
heard it.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.640
Bink's sake.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:18.970
And to my absolute astonishment, now that
I'm reading this again, the other island whales

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:24.529
recognise this song and actually start singing
as well, which is why they start carrying

00:12:24.529 --> 00:12:31.769
the sunny safely to the surface.

00:12:31.769 --> 00:12:37.420
Now in case you don't know why this is so
important, Binks sake is heavily connected

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.720
to Laugh Tale as well.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:45.460
The song literally ends with the phrase 'Never-Ending,
Ever-wandering, Our funny Traveling tale!',

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.430
using the Japanese kanji for laugh and tale.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:53.410
I actually made an entire video analysing
this song, that contains hints about the Kozuki,

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.720
the dawn of the world and much much more.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:13:02.050
Now I personally came to conclusion that Laugh
Tale might be the underworld, where the crew

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.580
would have to descend to.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:09.080
But now I actually believe that the underworld
is actually the bottom of the ocean, Davy

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:15.270
Jone's locker, the inside of a giant island
whale, to which the crew will have to descend.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.459
The ever-wandering laugh tale.

00:13:17.459 --> 00:13:21.800
That sounds a lot like a moving living thing,
similar to zuneshia.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:26.210
As you know from Luffy, Ace and Sabo, Sake
is a sign of brotherhood.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:31.700
So delivering binks sake to one of lagoons
brothers might be the promise that joy boy

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.930
made to the mermaid princess and that he could
never keep.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:35.930
The theme of siblings is closely connected
to the whales after all.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:40.750
There are also other lines in the song that
would fit well to laugh tale being under water.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.000
'If you lose your nerve this breath could
be your last.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.300
But if you just hold on, The morning sun will
rise.'

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.060
Holding your breath to go under water.

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:52.490
There is also Tsumugi no sato yo.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.960
Tsumugi no sato is the village of spinning.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:59.829
I originally thought that this refers to the
Kozuki spinning the history into the poneglyph.

00:13:59.829 --> 00:14:05.430
This is supported by 'The birds sing as they
draw circles in the sky!'

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:11.430
TO me that was probably the Kozuki crest,
but if Yuderon's idea is true and the whale

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:17.120
is trapped in the giant whirlpool between
the gates of justice, the spinning village

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:23.050
could literally be laugh tale caught in a
giant whirlpool, ever-moving.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:27.310
Before I tell you another crazy detail, if
you enjoy this type of content, the secret

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:31.329
to getting more of this every single week
is subscribing to the channel.

00:14:31.329 --> 00:14:36.149
Another crazy detail I found, is that there
is actually a Yokai in Japanese mythology

00:14:36.149 --> 00:14:40.279
called Bake-Kujira, a giant living whale skeleton.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:45.540
Now, Binks sake ends with, 'Doesn't matter
who you are, Someday you'll just be bones.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:47.860
Never-Ending, Ever-wandering, Our funny Traveling
tale!'

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:54.670
And we literally have brook, a living skeleton
that is connected to the island whales.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:59.580
Not sure if that's the direction Oda would
take this, but it might be relevant as well.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:05.950
But basically, the idea is, that a giant whale,
bit of laugh tale from Jaya 800 years ago

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:11.769
to protect whatever was there, but was trapped
by Imu and the government between 3 gates

00:15:11.769 --> 00:15:16.570
of justice at the bottom of the sea, where
it can not escape.

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:21.160
Which might be the reason why shanks and his
men all haven't eaten devil fruits, so they

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.930
can go and visit.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:27.980
After all shanks would well know how to get
to laugh tale, even if he stayed behind with

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.519
Buggy.

00:15:30.519 --> 00:15:37.460
Now as fascinating as this theory is, if you
really want to blow your own mind and take

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:41.110
it to the next level, this isn’t enough
on its own.

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:46.170
There is actually an absolutley crazy theory
about the true nature of laugh tale and the

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:51.269
ancient kingdom, that has changed how people
see one piece forever.

00:15:51.269 --> 00:15:55.240
And that’s why you really shouldnt ignore
this video, because it’s twice as exciting

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:59.950
as the whale theory and in combination with
it will make you feel like you’ve figured

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.040
out One Piece.

